      "pText": "Prime is the Sea Green twin-tower piece in our Pinnacle series. Two hexagonal tepee towers stand close together, joined by a rope net bridge, with green slides and a tube slide coming down and a climbing wall on one face. It is listed for 50 to 55 children at once. The product area is 35' x 27'7\", a broad footprint for a society lawn or an open patch in a park. Children use the bridge to swap towers and pick a different slide each time, which gets them playing in groups. Skills listed are exploring, confidence and social skills. Because it is one colour, Prime sits quietly in a landscaped garden. Cover for 3 years applies to the galvanised pipe, roto-moulded slides, laminates and play rope. Ask for a quote and a safe zone drawing."
